# XERJ index exclusions (gitignore syntax) for a standalone invesdwin-oss
# checkout.
#
# REDUNDANT WHEN INDEXED FROM ABOVE. .xerjignore outranks .gitignore and
# applies across submodule boundaries, so the workspace-root file in
# performancetrader-workspace already governs this tree when you index from
# there. This file exists for the developer who clones invesdwin-oss on its
# own, where nothing above it applies.
#
# Unlike the upper layers there is no market-data payload to prune here: this
# repo is pure source, with no cache/, log/ or doc/reference/ trees (those live
# in invesdwin-trading-test and invesdwin-trading-data, not here). What does
# occur is build output, IDE state, and binary payloads that ship inside the
# ~30 submodule dependencies — native libraries under dependencies/ta-lib,
# jars, and PDFs in docs.
#
# Anchoring: a gitignore pattern containing a slash is ANCHORED to the
# directory holding the ignore file, hence the `**/` where a rule must match at
# depth. Confirm with `xerj autoindex . --dry-run`, which prints one
# `.xerjignore:<rule> — N directories pruned` line per rule that fired.

# --- build output (also in XERJ's built-in list; explicit for clarity) ---
# `dependency/` is a build directory. It is NOT `dependencies/`, which holds
# real source submodules and must stay indexed.
target/
bin/
out/
dependency/

# --- IDE / editor ---
.idea/
*.iml
.metadata/
.vscode/
.project
.classpath
.settings/
.checkstyle
.factorypath
.springBeans
.nbproject
.attach_pid*
.jrctemp
.invesdwin
.activemq-data
.DS_Store

# --- binary + archive payloads ---
*.jar
*.war
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib
*.zip
*.tar
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.bin
*.dat
*.ser
*.jfr
*.db
*.sqlite
*.hprof

# --- logs and dumps ---
*.log
*.log[0-9]
hs_err_pid*.log
jacoco.exec

# --- data, not code ---
*.csv
*.pdf
